{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Like streams they stretch forth.</b> He mentioned here four expressions: כנחלים, כגנות, כאהלים, כארזים — and they correspond to the four banners that were in the wilderness, and these expressions are kinds of delight. And our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded in tractate Ta'anit: the good curse that Ahijah the Shilonite cursed Israel [was drawn] from the blessing of Balaam — for he blessed them with the cedar, for it says (Numbers 24:6): ״כארזים״ — while he cursed them with the reed, as it says (I Kings 14:15): ״והכה ה' את ישראל כאשר ינוד הקנה במים״ — for you find that the reeds sway to and fro, yet all the winds cannot uproot them from their place, and moreover their stock regrows; whereas he [Ahijah] cursed them with the reed, which sways — for every wind comes and bends it, and its stock does not regrow, and [Israel] are always swaying and tottering and never steadfast. And he said:"], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:35:44.144420201Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}